---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SplitSection from "../components/SplitSection.astro";
import AboutIntro from "../components/AboutIntro.astro";
import Appearances from "../components/Appearances.astro";
import { contactUrl } from "../data/site.js";
---

<Base title="About Niko Karppinen" description="Niko Karppinen is an SEO and analytics consultant working across digital measurement, technical implementation and practical digital systems." schemaPageType="about">
  <AboutIntro />

  <SplitSection id="approach" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>How I approach work</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        Good systems should make the next decision easier. That is usually the
        test I come back to, whether I am working on measurement, site structure,
        tracking, or something in between.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work often sits between SEO, analytics, content, tracking, and technical
        implementation. I look at how those areas connect rather than treating
        each one as a separate problem. Sometimes that also means questioning the
        problem itself. Are we solving the right thing, or have we accepted the
        original framing without checking it?
      </p>
      <p>
        When something feels abstract, I try to make it concrete. That might mean
        using examples, analogies, diagrams, or a small working model. I would
        rather build something that can be tested than leave behind a vague
        recommendation that sounds finished.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI can help apply a clear process more consistently. It does not fix bad
        source data, unclear ownership, or a process that nobody really
        understands.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am happy to automate the routine work, but decisions stay with people.
        I build checkpoints into workflows where someone reviews the result
        before it moves on.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <SplitSection id="values" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>What I care about</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        Measurement is worth the effort when someone makes a decision with it.
        Otherwise it is one more set of numbers to maintain.
      </p>
      <p>
        Good work should give people enough context to judge what is important
        and enough structure to act on it. Tools can surface patterns, but people
        still decide what matters for the customer, the business, and the brand.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <SplitSection id="background" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>Background</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        I have worked with SEO, analytics, and digital marketing since 2017.
        In that time, I have worked with organisations in ecommerce,
        telecommunications, insurance, healthcare, the public sector, B2B, and
        consumer services.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work has covered technical SEO, analytics and tracking implementations,
        consent setups, measurement planning, dashboards, website redesigns, and
        search-driven site structure planning.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have always been interested in how technology, content, structure,
        and storytelling fit together. I have also written short-film
        screenplays, because I enjoy working out how ideas, pacing, and
        communication shape each other.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <SplitSection id="outside-work" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>Outside work</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        In my free time, I watch films and anime and play story-driven
        single-player games. Alan Wake and Metal Gear Solid are among my
        favourites. I like well-built stories, strong atmosphere, and worlds
        that are a little strange.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also read comics, especially Batman and Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles.
        I am drawn to original ideas and to worlds that consistently follow
        their own rules.
      </p>
      <p>
        I dance Cuban salsa and locking. In both, I enjoy the rhythm, the
        practice, and the improvisation. Even a familiar move usually has
        something new to work on. I have learned to accept that I cannot do
        everything yet, and to enjoy the practice anyway.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <Appearances />

  <SplitSection id="how-i-write" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>How I write</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        I write about the work I do myself: analytics, tracking, search
        engine optimisation and using AI at work. I use AI when writing,
        but the thinking is my own. Every article shows its
        publish date at the top and, when the content has changed, the date
        it was updated.
      </p>
      <p>
        When a claim relies on an outside source, I link to the original,
        such as the vendor's own documentation. If an article's illustration
        was made with AI, the caption says so.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you spot a mistake or outdated information, let me know. I will
        fix it and update the article's updated date.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <SplitSection id="contact" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        The easiest way to reach me is LinkedIn. Send a message about working
        together, my work or the articles.
      </p>
      <p class="content-links"><a href={contactUrl} rel="me noopener">Message me on LinkedIn</a></p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>
</Base>
